# Lenovo Yoga Book 9 14IAH10 (83KJ) — accelerometer mount matrices
#
# Both accel IIO devices share the same modalias (platform:HID-SENSOR-200073)
# so hwdb cannot distinguish them — the second hwdb entry overwrites the first
# for both devices.  This rules file matches on DEVPATH instead, which includes
# the stable HID collection index (.12 / .13).
#
# Correct matrix for both: negate X only (-1,0,0; 0,1,0; 0,0,1).
# Verified by hardware test 2026-06-25 (indices .12/.13, kernel 7.0.x):
#   - Portrait tablet top-up:  raw_y positive → "normal"
#   - Portrait tablet bottom-up: raw_y negative → "bottom-up"
#   - Landscape right-up: raw_x negative → corr_x positive → "right-up"
#   - Landscape left-up:  raw_x positive → corr_x negative → "left-up"
#
# NOTE: kernel 7.1.3 renumbered HID collection indices from .12/.13 to .7/.8.
# Scale also changed: 1G ≈ 1,000,000 raw (was ≈1,031); in_accel_scale=9.806e-6.
#
# Supersedes /etc/udev/hwdb.d/61-sensor-yogabook9.hwdb (which has the bug
# but is left in place so it can be submitted upstream with corrections).

# Top screen section (eDP-1, iio:device0) — used by iio-sensor-proxy as primary
SUBSYSTEM=="iio", DEVPATH=="*HID-SENSOR-200073.7*", \
    ENV{ACCEL_MOUNT_MATRIX}="-1, 0, 0; 0, 1, 0; 0, 0, 1"

# Base/bottom section (eDP-2, iio:device2)
# iio-sensor-proxy selects the lower-numbered device (.7 = iio:device0) as
# primary, so .8 does not interfere.  yoga9-rotate reads .8 Y-axis for tent mode.
SUBSYSTEM=="iio", DEVPATH=="*HID-SENSOR-200073.8*", \
    ENV{ACCEL_MOUNT_MATRIX}="-1, 0, 0; 0, 1, 0; 0, 0, 1"
